# Benchmark change 07: per-kernel launch and fallback counts. Instrumentation only.
# Reason: inject.py swallows kernel exceptions and falls back to PyTorch, and decode-step attention always runs PyTorch
# SDPA by design. "KERNEL_*=ACTIVE" only meant "injected", so no result could show which kernels actually ran (Opus's
# final review, criterion 3).
# Change: inject.py counts each wrapped op's custom-kernel calls and fallbacks, keeps the first exception per op, and
# counts decode-step attention as PyTorch. bench.py resets the counts before each timed benchmark and prints and records
# them (BASELINE_KERNEL_COUNTS, KERNEL_COUNTS, KERNEL_FALLBACKS). Return values are unchanged, and nothing feeds the
# score or the correctness check.
# Approved: PLAN Amendment (20) item 2. Test: test_instrumentation_07.py (CPU).
#
